# arenagen specification for pats_staexp2.{sats,dats}: the level-2 static syntax (--compact)
# python3 ../utils/arenagen/arenagen.py --global sats pats_staexp2.spec > pats_staexp2_gen.hats
# python3 ../utils/arenagen/arenagen.py --global --compact dats pats_staexp2.spec > pats_staexp2_gen_dats.hats
#
# Same conventions as pats_syntax.spec / pats_staexp1.spec ([record R (f: T, ..)] is a flat record R_new(..), x.f();
# [type N] is a datatype N_CON(..) with N_view for pattern matching; List/Option are glist/gopt).
#
# New here: [mut f: T] marks a field of a record that is assigned after the creation (generates set_f (x, v)).
# These records are the cells of ATS1 that were [ref (struct)]: s2rtdat, s2rtVar, s2cst, s2var, s2Var, d2con.
# They are allocated in the global arena and never freed; their address is their identity (a cell never moves).
#
# The ATS1 boxed tuples, not allowed in the no-GC rules, are records: syms2rt (symbol, s2rt), locs2exp (location, s2exp),
# d2conpair (the Option@(d2con, d2con) of s2cst_islst). The one-constructor datatypes SLABELED, SKLABELED, SZLABELED
# are the records labs2exp, labs2kexp, labs2zexp (like labs1exp).
# The field [s2Var_svar] of ATS1 (no getter or setter exists, always None) is dropped; [s2cst_arylst] is kept.
# A "null" s2rt in [s2rtVar_srt] means unset (the s2rtnul of pats_staexp2_sort.dats).
#
# The sets are persistent AVL trees of pats_avlmap.sats: the field types s2Varset, s2varset.. are abstypes of the sats.
typedef s2rtlst = glist(s2rt)
typedef s2rtopt = gopt(s2rt)
typedef s2rtlstlst = glist(s2rtlst)
typedef s2rtlstopt = gopt(s2rtlst)
